  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Lateral entry MBA in India means direct admission into the second year of a 2-year MBA or PGDM program, skipping the first year, usually for candidates who already completed year 1 of a related postgraduate program elsewhere, or who bring specific work experience an institute recognises.</strong>
    If you came here expecting the far more common meaning of "lateral entry" in India — diploma holders
    joining a BTech directly in year 2 — that is a different, nationally standardised engineering scheme,
