  <h2 id="next-step">What to do next</h2>

  <p>
    Do not decide this from a college's marketing page alone, and do not assume the term means what the
    much more common BTech lateral-entry route means.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      If a genuine lateral-entry MBA fits your situation, verify the institute's UGC/AICTE standing for
      that exact program, get the equivalence claim in writing, and compare the real time saved against
      the recognition risk before you commit.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>If the honest answer is that you do not have a firm, specific reason to rush, a well-placed
      regular 2-year MBA or a genuine Executive MBA usually protects your income and career options
      better than a faster but less verified route</strong> — the goal is a stronger, high-income skill
      portfolio and earlier financial freedom, not just a shorter timetable.
    </p>
  </div>

